  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Guardrail (ADR-0017, closes Critical Finding #1)",
      "items": [
        "The LLM-summarized feedback is never passed directly to Findings Author — it surfaces as its own reviewable artifact, and only Lead/Approver confirmation triggers the redraft",
        "Closes the gap where an ungrounded AI summary could change a regulatory document on something no human actually said. \"Approved\" needs no elaboration (decision 103) and isn't drawn here"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Diagram scope",
      "items": [
        "The pre-exit concerns loop reuses this exact redraft/sign-off flow rather than a separate \"Exit Deck\" screen (decision 105)",
        "Full states: drafted → awaiting_ag → changes_requested → ag_feedback_reviewed → redraft → awaiting_ag → approved"
      ]
    }
  ]
